// ============================================================
//  DO NOT DEPLOY OR "FIX" THIS FILE WITHOUT READING THIS BLOCK
// ============================================================
//
// This file MIRRORS the rules currently LIVE in production.
// They are FULLY OPEN: anyone can read and write all data.
//
// This is NOT the intended end state. It is a deliberate snapshot
// of reality, kept here so that source matches production and a
// stray `firebase deploy` cannot change behaviour.
//
// WHY THE PREVIOUS CONTENTS WERE REMOVED:
// The old contents of this file (see git history) were never
// deployed and CANNOT be. They gate on an isOwner() custom claim
// that is set NOWHERE in the codebase, and read resource.data
// .ownerId while every writer uses ownerUid. Deploying them would
// break ~10 of 12 core flows and lock every clinic out of its own
// data.
//
// THE REAL RULES ARE BLOCKED ON THREE THINGS:
//   1. Owner custom claims (role + clinicId) — never issued today.
//   2. Doctor Firebase Auth — doctors currently have NO Firebase
//      Auth session at all (login compares a plaintext password
//      field in Firestore), so ANY rule requiring
//      request.auth != null locks out every doctor.
//   3. Patient Firebase Auth — patients sign in with a 6-digit code
//      and have no Firebase Auth session either.
//
// Until those land, tightening these rules WILL take the app down.
// Do NOT hand-edit this file to "improve security".
//
// LAUNCH BLOCKER: no real clinic may onboard while these rules are
// live. Today, anyone can read every doctor's plaintext password,
// grant themselves a free subscription, hijack any clinic, and
// read or delete all patient data.
// ============================================================
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    //  DEVELOPMENT MODE - OPEN ACCESS
    // WARNING: This allows anyone to read/write all data
    // Use only for development/testing
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if true;
    }
  }
}
